A||||22||Scott2M4||Loud noise from HVAC system||||5||
Z||000000||Scott2M4||12-06-1999||12:50 PM||||The rain we got this weekend prompted me to use the "defrost" setting on the HVAC controls for the first time since I bought the car in November.<P>Ready to leave for work this morning, I fired up the car, hit the "defrost" button, and out of nowhere came a   T H W A P!   Or was it a   F W A C K!?   Well, the air began flowing onto the windshield following the loud noise and I didn't need my morning cup of coffee either!!!!!  I did, however, need to change my shorts!<P>Ideas?  Suggestions?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||12-06-1999||01:40 PM||||Check your air conditioner pump belt. The pump kicks on with the dsefrost||||reg||1
Z||000002||Scott2M4||12-06-1999||03:29 PM||||The noise comes from under (or behind) the center of the dash.  It sounds like plastic slamming against plastic.||||reg||1
Z||000003||peterh||12-06-1999||03:56 PM||||I get a loud wack noise whenever I push the vent button on my car too. I think it is the doors changing where the air flows. Hopefully nothing too worry about.||||reg||1
Z||000004||jlhuber||12-06-1999||06:17 PM||||my 86 is the same way ... is that bad?||||reg||1
Z||000005||MCordray||12-06-1999||07:01 PM||||My '86 does the same thing. I think mine has something to do with a heater core that went bad. It ended up spilling coolant inside the vents. The THWACK sound may be where old coolant is still sticky, causing the vent door to slam once it's freed from the old, sticky coolant. But, that's just a guess...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||12-06-1999||08:06 PM||||Try to switch from heat to defrost in any other car and you'll probably hear the same noise.  Mine does it and so does my wifes' car and she has a '98 Cavalier.  It should make a similar sound when you switch back to something else.||||reg||1
Z||000007||william_thorniii||12-06-1999||08:41 PM||||Scott,<P>You are in the Dayton area right????  If so I can stop by and you can listen to my 87 SC.  Unless you are lucky and I happen to be driving my 85 GT that day... then you just get to listen to that one instead.  They both make the T H W A C K... but the 87's is louder... although I think mine is more of a T H U U U M M P <P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>937-259-5295 (work)||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||12-06-1999||08:59 PM||||I have an '88, and mine doesn't "thwak".  I can however, hear the door motor moving. It goes "rruurruurr". Kinda soft, but you can hear it if the radio is off.<P>At least you guys get to drive your Fieros.  It's been two weeks, of working, waiting, and breaking stuff.  I miss my car, wish that slave cylinder had'nt broke...<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 12-06-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Scott2M4||12-06-1999||09:13 PM||||Wow!  And I thought my car was special ... you know, one of those rare HVAC systems that REALLY lets you know when it's changing modes!  Hell, I was even thinking about selling my system on Ebay for a ton of money (right next to those sun shades!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   )<P>Well cool!  Sounds like it's not something to worry about.  Thanks, folks.<P>William - yes, I'm in the Dayton area (Springboro to be exact).||||reg||4
Z||000010||Phil||12-06-1999||09:48 PM||||There was a thread awhile back about a malfuntioning goink suppressor- sounds like the thwacker stops could be having the same kind of trouble||||reg||1
Z||000011||ka4nkf||12-06-1999||10:31 PM||||Glad to hear i am not the only one with this noise. mine is very loud.||||reg||1
Z||000012||batboy||12-06-1999||11:16 PM||||Fiero air exchanger doors are a little noisy, but mine never made me wet my pant.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I remember an old magazine article (maybe Car and Driver) where they complained that it was noisy even back when they were new.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Standard||12-07-1999||01:52 AM||||<B>goink suppressor</B>? <B>thwacker stops</B>?  Are these related to the <B>blue dingy thingy</B>?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 12-07-1999).]||||reg||10
