Z||000015||DJRice||12-07-1999||09:03 AM||||So did we ever figure out what causes the <B>Kajungas</B>?||||reg||1
Z||000016||LMH87SC5||12-08-1999||07:48 PM||||Wife of Scott2M4 here... Noise scared the heck out of me on my way to work!  Might have been a good idea to mention... cause now we need to wash two sets of shorts!||||reg||11
Z||000017||theogre||12-08-1999||08:01 PM||||You should hear the motors run as the heater changes the dampers positions. Other noises indicate binding dampers. Fix these or you could break the motor modules. No, fixing the dampers isn't easy.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Monkeyman||12-09-1999||12:57 AM||||Standard--I believe it's "blue chimy thingy"!<P>You can eliminate the Kajungas completely if you remove the top of the Snarfilation valve and deflate the wizamacram on the Popasnoogle.  I thought everyone knew this.  But this only works if you whamalamadingdong the knarknar with the Hofmeister option.  Just wanted to clarify that.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Standard||12-09-1999||01:34 AM||||If I remember right it's <B>blue dingy thingy</B>.  Do a search!  And thanks for clearing all that up, Monkey! Maybe now I can get my car to run right... damn malfunctioning Snarfilation valves...||||reg||12
Z||000020||Monkeyman||12-09-1999||07:19 PM||||No prob.  It's all in the Whatchamacallit Book (Vol. 3, of course).  Look under the section entitled,"Thingamabobs, Dodads, and Doogifloppers".||||reg||1
Z||000021||Richard Parnell||12-09-1999||07:48 PM||||Mine does the same, it's because of da kine.||||reg||6
Z||000022||87GT||12-09-1999||09:43 PM||||I think this is pretty funny.  I hit any button to turn on anything and all it does is make winding noises for a few seconds and then I have air blowing.  I go to turn it off and the winding starts up again and then air stops.. It works well but the winding noise is kinda loud.  I have learned to ignore it and was reminded of it when I decided to read this post. hehehhehe||||reg||1
